\title{detfield: Detection Fields and Location Surfaces for Acoustic Telemetry}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Builds detection-efficiency fields for fixed acoustic receiver arrays from a fitted range model and distances measured through water, and turns detection counts into location surfaces: for each tagged animal and time bin, the probability that the animal was in each water cell. The surface for a bin is a posterior over water cells from a binomial likelihood of the detection counts of every listening receiver, with the spread of each receiver's detection probability within a time bin given as an argument. Credible regions and samples drawn from the surfaces feed habitat and movement analyses.
